9. In Ram Prasad Singh v. King Emperor, ILR 1 Pat 753 : (AIR 1923 Pat 50), the head note is as follows;
"Where the principal offender in a case of rioting is convicted of an offence the others cannot be held to have committed constructively an offence different from the offence found to have been committed by the principal offender.
Therefore, where the principal offender was convicted under Section 302, held, that the others could not be convicted under Section 304 read with Section 149."

13. But in the same volume, there is another case at page 242 of AIR 1946 Pat.;
Ram Charan Rai v. Emperor
, where preference is indicated for the view expressed in Ram Prasad Singh's case, ILR 1 Pat 753 : (AIR 1923 Pat 50).
